    description:
      "Attachment security priming — briefly recalling or visualising a relationship in which you felt safe and cared for — reliably shifts mood, expectations and prosocial behaviour in laboratory studies, and a systematic review found supraliminal primes, especially guided visualisation, had beneficial effects that were strongest for anxiously attached people. Repeated priming over days produced more positive views of self and relationships that persisted, and priming raised compassion and willingness to help. The effects are modest and often transient, so the protocol is a cheap pre-date ritual, not a cure for insecure attachment.",
